{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons","id":109497,"title":"Summoning Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-09T11:49:15-07:00","id":109497,"title":"Summoning Demons","content":"Something that has been annoying me. There are no rules to summon demons. Summoning demons is VERY iconic to demons and are practically synonymous with demons. I mean, why hunt down people to make deals when people are calling you(summoning) up themselves to make deals? I think a lot of game potential is missing by not including it. Would love to see something cover this in a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T11:53:03-07:00","id":109502,"title":"","content":"I'd rather let my cultist -THINK- they can summon me rather than this being the case. That aside, there could be Glitches to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T12:09:09-07:00","id":109517,"title":"","content":"Here's the question you should be asking yourself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why would a demon have a power to summon another demon? <i>Mortals</i> (such as mages and hunters and the ilk) have summoning rituals. This is a game about playing a demon, the one who would be summoned. Not the one who is doing the summoning.<br /> <br /> So, now its my turn to ask. &quot;What potential is missing?&quot; <br /> <br /> Seriously. Other than &quot;demons are summoned,&quot; what's missing here? Why would it support or help as playing a demon/fallen angel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T12:21:48-07:00","id":109536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons#post109497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that has been annoying me. There are no rules to summon demons. Summoning demons is VERY iconic to demons and are practically synonymous with demons. I mean, why hunt down people to make deals when people are calling you(summoning) up themselves to make deals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because having a perfectly reliable call-number is such an egregious violation of the Moscow Rules' sixth and ninth bullet points that the list virtually catches fire.<br /> <br /> Also because &quot;someone has a job for you to do&quot; is the headspace that <i>angels</i> occupy and literally any demon with two Experiences to drop can produce a cell phone. (I find myself wondering if &quot;call the nearest phone to a target&quot; is an Embed that the Player's Guide will have.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T12:26:33-07:00","id":109549,"title":"","content":"Its evocative, the whole summoning ritual for a bargain brings a lot cool imagery and invokes a lot of stories.<br /> <br /> But why not embeds or exploits for demons to show up when called, make traveling to where called easier, or twist fate so they stumble upon folks calling them. I can't remember but wasn't there some sort of power that Demons could buy that allowed them to notice when people talk about them? It was a thing in Fallen that was pretty cool where Demons heard other Demons after they spoke their name.<br /> <br /> But on another angle what about a power to summon lesser demons, like techno-imps, gremlins, and those clockwork Gnome things mentioned sometimes having to do with the god machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T12:54:40-07:00","id":109568,"title":"","content":"It also deserves mention that the iconic demon-summoning sorcerers, Faustian deals, imp servitors, etc is covered by another game in the line: <i>Inferno</i>. While you make a good point that being summoned would be an easy way for Demons (of the Descent) to make pacts, Descent uses very different themes, conceptions, and implications of demons than those kinds of stories.<br /> <br /> Demon summoners usually evoke themes of hubris, domination, playing with forces you can't control, desperation for power corrupting the soul; to be one of those demons would evoke enslavement, slowly undermining a foolish master, manipulation of human emotion and motives, and desire to have an impact in the mortal world which can only be gained through whispers, lies, and captivity [themes which <i>almost</i> kind of resonate more with Changeling, in my opinion]. It would be much more in line with Descent's themes to spy on mortals doing this kind of research, feeding them false information, and using various tricks to show up <i>instead</i> of the entity they wanted and play to their expectations in order to snag a Cover. Its trickier and more difficult, but it can be arranged, and, I think, more thematically appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T13:11:09-07:00","id":109575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109568#post109568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> to be one of those demons would evoke enslavement, slowly undermining a foolish master, manipulation of human emotion and motives, and desire to have an impact in the mortal world which can only be gained through whispers, lies, and captivity [themes which <i>almost</i> kind of resonate more with Changeling, in my opinion].</div> </div> </div> </div> Playing someone's servant and being tugged around by a master is a very difficult game to play. And that's what would end up happening, I think. Games of summoning demons are played from the summoner's perspective, like Inferno, and rarely from the summonee's. Mummy is the closest in my opinion, with how they're summoned by their cult, and driven by their necromancer-god masters.<br /> <br /> Now, I suppose we could get rules for that kind of thing in the future but I don't see it as very conductive to long term play. For one, you would need stuff to do when not slaving for your master (Mummies tend to sleep or try to take over the world). And you'd need something to allow group play - few summoners want to call up multiple demons at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, it can be done. I just really think it needs its own chapter and considerations beyond the core. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-09-2014, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T13:47:21-07:00","id":109604,"title":"","content":"Summoning, not binding. There are ton of stories about stupid people finding a rituals, or an old summoning circle, or hear a rumor about a way to summon a demon (crossroads demon like in supernatural) to get you what you want. Supernatural is actually a good example, no demon was ever a servant, they were summoned to make a deal, but were never bound. They usually did not just do the deal and leave, they often stuck around to make more deals to the horror of the original person who summoned them.<br /> <br /> There is also no reason that only one demon is summoned, going with the trope of stupid people finding a ritual to jokingly &quot;summon&quot; some demons, they would be surprised when it actually summons multiple demons within the circle. This could be a start of a game. Or you can have a rumor spread that doing this ritual you can summon a demon to get what you want. This would be a good way for NPC's to make contact with a demon without having some convoluted story about a character discovering they are demons. <br /> <br /> While the DTD might have different themes (which should have not been so narrow, but that is another complaint for another time), it still easily fits in. Someone finds out an &quot;angel&quot; is doing something horrible to their town, they do research and find a way of summoning a &quot;devil&quot; to fight the angel..etc. <br /> <br /> Even if its just used for NPC demons, at least there will be rules for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T14:46:26-07:00","id":109634,"title":"","content":"Yeah but in your example it's well within the mindset of Demon to lead &quot;Stupid people&quot; on a goose chase and &quot;uncover&quot; a &quot;ritual&quot; and then pop out when it climaxes. Having rules for strategy takes an aspect out of the game doesn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T14:58:59-07:00","id":109640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109634#post109634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but in your example it's well within the mindset of Demon to lead &quot;Stupid people&quot; on a goose chase and &quot;uncover&quot; a &quot;ritual&quot; and then pop out when it climaxes. Having rules for strategy takes an aspect out of the game doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus we're talking about a splat whose powers are fairly easy to turn to the end of starting exploitable urban legends. It's hardly difficult to get the word out that if you go to the broken-down motel out by the edge of town at 3:33am on a Tuesday with a pack of cigarettes the Dark Lady will give you her patronage when you can literally plant ideas in people's heads with minimal investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T15:17:22-07:00","id":109645,"title":"","content":"Summoning is directly opposed to the central themes of D:tD. Demons are supposed to be stupidly hard to find, much less pin down. If Demons could be summoned, forcibly and directly you can bet that 90% of those summoners would be G-M agents with ample Angelic presence.<br /> <br /> Seraph Kitty has it right that any 'Summoning' in Decent would stem from an active plot, set in motion deliberately by the Demon in order to acquire soul pacts (or lead Angels astray, or undermind infrastructure, or recruit stigmatics, or some other cockamamie scheme). And it'd probably be more akin to &quot;Tune your television to channel X at exactly 12:34am on Tuesday&quot; than the more commonly conceived of occult rituals. (Though that's not to say a Demon couldn't set up a fake ritual, he could totally do that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T15:56:15-07:00","id":109667,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about forcing the demon to it? I was thinking summoning is more like a phone call. Demons can hear it, but whether they answer it or not is up to them. I was thinking that demons might get an advantage over the summoner that makes accepting a call like this worth it. Like automatically getting hearts desires specifically for the summoner and a few other things. Saves a lot of time and effort.<br /> <br /> I find it sad that if you want more traditional demon tropes in a game called DEMONS that &quot;your playing it wrong&quot;. That is just messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T15:56:49-07:00","id":109668,"title":"","content":"Conversely, we DO have summoning rituals for Angels, who do look pretty evil at times. Translucent flesh, fangs, claws, sword arms...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T18:34:23-07:00","id":109750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109517#post109517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the question you should be asking yourself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why would a demon have a power to summon another demon? <i>Mortals</i> (such as mages and hunters and the ilk) have summoning rituals. This is a game about playing a demon, the one who would be summoned. Not the one who is doing the summoning.<br /> <br /> So, now its my turn to ask. &quot;What potential is missing?&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously. Other than &quot;demons are summoned,&quot; what's missing here? Why would it support or help as playing a demon/fallen angel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im most occult lore demons want to be summoned, no less so in Descent. I imagine rules for this will be forthcomming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T23:40:52-07:00","id":109892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109668#post109668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, we DO have summoning rituals for Angels, who do look pretty evil at times. Translucent flesh, fangs, claws, sword arms...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason why all biblical angelic encounters begin with &quot;Be Not Afraid&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T00:47:20-07:00","id":109946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversely, we DO have summoning rituals for Angels, who do look pretty evil at times. Translucent flesh, fangs, claws, sword arms... </div> </div> </div>I don\u00b4t remember that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T03:18:58-07:00","id":109986,"title":"","content":"In Soviet Russia, Demons summon you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T04:34:52-07:00","id":110011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109750#post109750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im most occult lore demons want to be summoned, no less so in Descent. I imagine rules for this will be forthcomming.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that being summoned very likely includes a hefty Compromise check... and one that's not within your control? I can't imagine that it would be too popular.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109986#post109986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Soviet Russia, Demons summon you!</div> </div> </div> </div> Or, you know, any Demon with the Summon Exploit. Which, to be honest, is rather... weak overall. &quot;Person happens to come to you as part of their daily routine,&quot; isn't what I call magic worthy of Exploit level; if anything, this is worth being knocked down to Embed level, preferably as a Mundane embed - psychopomps need some actual &quot;I move people around&quot; powers. Its also entirely coincidental, the type of thing that fits the subtle manipulation of being a spy. <br /> <br /> Now, I could see using an Exploit as an actual &quot;I teleport you wherever you are to me!&quot; thing. I don't know why the writers like the old Presence/Majesty 4 power - its a pretty lame one, over all. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:05:33-07:00","id":110139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=109640#post109640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus we're talking about a splat whose powers are fairly easy to turn to the end of starting exploitable urban legends. It's hardly difficult to get the word out that if you go to the broken-down motel out by the edge of town at 3:33am on a Tuesday with a pack of cigarettes the Dark Lady will give you her patronage when you can literally plant ideas in people's heads with minimal investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>What power lets you do that? I have been reading my book and can't find anything like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:11:23-07:00","id":110145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=110139#post110139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What power lets you do that? I have been reading my book and can't find anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Plant ideas in people's heads&quot; is a fairly direct description of Muse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T16:34:31-07:00","id":110398,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of summoning lesser demons, anything from hellhounds to lesser NPC demons. As for being summoned, like I said, demons should get something out of it besides just a simple bargain. Something that makes the risk worth it. Ok, here is a thought, so lets say someone does a ritual that summons a demon. The demon &quot;hears&quot; the call. Now, they have two choices, they can ignore it and nothing will happen, or they can answer it and see who is on the other line. Now, some of the benefits could be they automatically get specific embeds/exploits for this person/situation. Ok, say they get alibi, so instead of the demon actually telephoning themselves to the circle, they can send one of their covers (if they have more than one) instead to do the willing and dealing while the real demon is nice and safe. Worse case scenario is an angel is waiting and the demon loses a cover. Secondly, the demon could automatically get hearts desires so they automatically know what the person really wants. <br /> <br /> Now, flip it around for another game line, you want to make contact with a DTD demon to make a deal, how would you do it? They are all in hiding and unless they are idiots, they cover their tracks pretty well. Summoning is the most common anwser that comes to mind. Look up specific information/rituals on how to summon the demon. Find out what draws it, its nature. Do the ritual and hope the demon shows up. <br /> <br /> On a side note, As mentioned, an exploit that can hear their name being mentioned and/or summoning would be cool. So some demons could be summoned and others could not. The spreading rumor is cool and has a lot of potential, but like I said. Summoning is so iconic for demons that summoning practically means demons because that is usually what is summoned. I just think it would add a lot to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T17:25:07-07:00","id":110423,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect that rules for this might show up in the Demon Translation Guide since summoning was possible in DtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T11:06:05-07:00","id":110930,"title":"","content":"Regarding summoning a player character in game: I DO think that it could be powerful experience for a player and her character, just so you know. The notion of finding oneself arriving \u2013 via one's one power or by *poof* magic \u2013 at a mere mortal's call, that cuts to the bone of any number of <b>Demon: the Descent</b> themes. Maybe it won't work for all troupes, but I can absolutely see some usefulness to rules on such a thing. Add in the idea that these fallen angels of the God-Machine call themselves 'demons' in the first place, the connexion to summoned spirits may not be accidental. There's plenty of possible evidence that no angel falls without the God-Machine's permission (well, depending upon whom one believes, of course!), and the investigation of HOW such a summons works and WHY is brilliant techgnostic investigation material.<br /> <br /> ...Nah, I don't think that the game NEEDS these rules, but they absolutely do fit. Mileage varies and whatnot, so nobody need take my 2p as anything too serious. Actually, I just wrote a really interesting story of a game, above, that can work without said rules being fully disclosed. Go ahead, feel free to swipe it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:21:56-07:00","id":111202,"title":"","content":"Summoning demons, and in a broader sense the trappings of demonology as a whole, are one of the more evocative parts of dealing with things called &quot;demons&quot;, and I was initially somewhat bummed that the Unchained touch on it very lightly if at all. I definitely know where the OP's coming from. That said, I understand how it just really kinda doesn't work with the way the Unchained work and the genre tropes that are central to it's core themes, and I feel like as a whole what I got more than makes up for that omission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:50:49-07:00","id":111219,"title":"","content":"In any case, I now have to add &quot;call-center Messenger&quot; to my list of Ciphers to develop.<br /> <br /> Tempter proxy-Interlocks will be the death of me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:53:04-07:00","id":111220,"title":"","content":"Demon summonning is an iconic and cool thing...from the point of view of the summoner.<br /> <br /> From the demonic perspective, simply being able to be summoned is actually a little inconvenient. Better still for them is to know when someone's will is tugging on the web of their existence, especially as a sign of giving in, and being able to respond quickly to that moment of weakness. Variations thereof apply.<br /> <br /> I'd almost make a merit/exploit out of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:56:12-07:00","id":111223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=111220#post111220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon summonning is an iconic and cool thing...from the point of view of the summoner.<br /> <br /> From the demonic perspective, simply being able to be summoned is actually a little inconvenient. Better still for them is to know when someone's will is tugging on the web of their existence, especially as a sign of giving in, and being able to respond quickly to that moment of weakness. Variations thereof apply.<br /> <br /> I'd almost make a merit/exploit out of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the mention of tricks in the Player's Guide like being able to turn into data and move through fiber optics will be particularly helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T05:22:39-07:00","id":111408,"title":"","content":"Well, I've considered that kind of teleportation stuff before, moving through wires. However.... that's like moving through Infrastructure! Kind of a worrysome Compromise check, I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm just not really sure how the whole summoning thing would work. Like I said before, there's the Summon Exploit, but that's not something I would use normally. Hells, given that its mundane travel by foot, and only on humans, I'd say that its not that impressive of a power. Good for the Tempter who's cultivating pacts, or arranging deals, but its not exactly something that's exceedingly pressing to get around in a lot of cases. <br /> <br /> <br /> There's not a lot of powers in the WoD as a whole that let you teleport large distances. Mage is the only one I know that does it simply with an exertion of will, and that's a Mastery level effect. Changelings have a few &quot;run through the Hedge quickly&quot; stuff. Hmm... well, there IS that one Guilded Cage ritual too. But, other than that... <br /> <br /> <br /> Its just that there's a lot that needs to be addressed, not to mention that the whole True Name thing doesn't apply to Unchained, which is another problem. How do you summon a demon by its name... when the Fallen don't have names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-12-2014, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T13:19:22-07:00","id":111721,"title":"","content":"Being able to be summoned is a useful power to have, not just for the Summoner. I admit, I did a custom power (its an NPC so I'm not sure if its an Exploit or Propulsion) that let's a Demon set up summoning conditions for them self. When the conditions are met, the demon gets to see the summoning area and choose to answer or not. It's useful because it removes the need to locate the target, eliminates the risk of physical travel, and can be turned down. Downsides are that the Summon doesn't have a return trip, and disguises/ambushes are still possible. To cut down on potential accidents (ie summoner is fine, but the only exit of the room leads to angels), the demon has to be careful who knows how to summon him. Still, its an impressive way to start the negociations for Pacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:17:03-07:00","id":111755,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MCN: Considering that being summoned very likely includes a hefty Compromise check... and one that's not within your control? I can't imagine that it would be too popular. </div> </div> </div>Mechanics already exist in Requiem for this, I would not see why equivalents could not exist in Demon, it does lend itself to the themes of paranoia and espionage the game aspires to.<br /> <br /> I could see this particularly for mortals or other Demons acquiring knowledge of one's True Name.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T03:06:01-07:00","id":111976,"title":"","content":"To add my two cents to the summon exploit. It is weak and should not be an exploit at all. In most cases, you could easily get most people to where you want them with a simple phone call and a good excuse. If that does not work there are usually a lot of easier ways to pull it off without any powers at all. This should be an (I agree about mundane) embed at best, for an exploit you should actually teleport the target to your location.<br /> <br /> As for summoning (teleporting) demons, I have to disagree that it does not fit the game. Otherwise, how can you have CULTS in the game, but not summoning? They kind of go hand in hand really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=111721#post111721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to be summoned is a useful power to have, not just for the Summoner. I admit, I did a custom power (its an NPC so I'm not sure if its an Exploit or Propulsion) that let's a Demon set up summoning conditions for them self. When the conditions are met, the demon gets to see the summoning area and choose to answer or not. It's useful because it removes the need to locate the target, eliminates the risk of physical travel, and can be turned down. Downsides are that the Summon doesn't have a return trip, and disguises/ambushes are still possible. To cut down on potential accidents (ie summoner is fine, but the only exit of the room leads to angels), the demon has to be careful who knows how to summon him. Still, its an impressive way to start the negociations for Pacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much what I was thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","user":"Badmojo","date":". 04-13-2014, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T03:07:13-07:00","id":111977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=111755#post111755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mechanics already exist in Requiem for this, I would not see why equivalents could not exist in Demon, it does lend itself to the themes of paranoia and espionage the game aspires to. I could see this particularly for mortals or other Demons acquiring knowledge of one's True Name.</div> </div> </div> </div> Requiem's version of summoning other PC is to psychically compel them to journey to you, an effect reproduced by the Summon Exploit. Vampires may summon their spiritual counterparts, the strix, with magic. Demons could, in theory, summon angels, but that tends to lead to death. Using optional even for a supplement (optional sidebar), outdated (Blasphemies and Sacraments forbids this) rules, a vampire might call a Hisil spirit, but that lacks the teleportation aspects one would need for a demon summoning to work. Also, unchained have no name by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T10:54:40-07:00","id":112118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=111977#post111977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Requiem's version of summoning other PC is to psychically compel them to journey to you, an effect reproduced by the Summon Exploit. Vampires may summon their spiritual counterparts, the strix, with magic. Demons could, in theory, summon angels, but that tends to lead to death. Using optional even for a supplement (optional sidebar), outdated (Blasphemies and Sacraments forbids this) rules, a vampire might call a Hisil spirit, but that lacks the teleportation aspects one would need for a demon summoning to work. Also, unchained have no name by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies doesn't forbid calling a normal Hisil spirit, so long as they're on this side of the guantlet. However, summoning a spirit is now riskier by what I believe David Hill was saying, as your more likely to get a Strix if not calling for a specific spirit. The prohibition on other realms is based on creating portals and shaping other realms, not summoning their inhabitants.<br /> <br /> A vampire may very well be able to summon an Angel, so long as its already here somewhere.<br /> <br /> Its been discussed a number of times what that passage meant, and I've followed those threads from the old forums and here rather extensively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T13:48:49-07:00","id":112217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=112118#post112118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies doesn't forbid calling a normal Hisil spirit, so long as they're on this side of the guantlet. However, summoning a spirit is now riskier by what I believe David Hill was saying, as your more likely to get a Strix if not calling for a specific spirit. The prohibition on other realms is based on creating portals and shaping other realms, not summoning their inhabitants.<br /> <br /> A vampire may very well be able to summon an Angel, so long as its already here somewhere.<br /> <br /> Its been discussed a number of times what that passage meant, and I've followed those threads from the old forums and here rather extensively.</div> </div> </div> </div> That may be, but no matter how you spin it, vampires don't summon anything physical body with a &quot;teleportation into a magic circle&quot; effect, which was what I was all I was trying to say. <br /> <br /> If vampires could summon other vampires, then we'd be talking about something to cross over. The whole demon-summoner thing has a lot of issues with it, as well as the fact that its not exactly a story that works with a full ring of demons as much. You almost need an entire game devoted to it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T16:53:36-07:00","id":112321,"title":"","content":"Why not simply say that summoning actually activates one of the many hidden subroutines that the GM wrote into reality. For whatever reason, the GM won't stop it or can't see its being used to summon demons (and other things). It can be one of the mysteries why normal people, demons, and other supernatural can use it, but angles cannot. <br /> <br /> As for groups, I can easily see uses for it. No reason only one demon may be called. A powerful demon creates a summons and sends out a call to multiple demons for unknown purposes with promises of high level covers and other things of value, perhaps something specific of value to each individual demon, they all agree and poof, your circle is filled with demons (group) from all over and you have the start of a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T17:25:16-07:00","id":112336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=112321#post112321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not simply say that summoning actually activates one of the many hidden subroutines that the GM wrote into reality. For whatever reason, the GM won't stop it or can't see its being used to summon demons (and other things). It can be one of the mysteries why normal people, demons, and other supernatural can use it, but angles cannot. As for groups, I can easily see uses for it. No reason only one demon may be called. A powerful demon creates a summons and sends out a call to multiple demons for unknown purposes with promises of high level covers and other things of value, perhaps something specific of value to each individual demon, they all agree and poof, your circle is filled with demons (group) from all over and you have the start of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would actually be a pretty awesome way to start a game, and an idea for a chronicle--a cult of demon summoners, through various means (such as teleporting demons, summonable exploits, and the coincidental &quot;summoning&quot; of demons discussed earlier), has bound several demons via pacts. They're all called together, and almost forced to become a ring by the actions of the summoners. Summoning and such would come up often, in all the different ways discussed above. It could be a fun, flavourful game, and could help some people who aren't into techgnosis feel a more distinct &quot;demonic&quot; vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T06:34:24-07:00","id":112588,"title":"","content":"I'm sold. That's a pretty cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:49:53-07:00","id":112884,"title":"","content":"Or another thought - the GM has cults perform rituals all the time for different reasons. So do these rituals simply stop working when the cult moves on? No. If someone picks up the ritual and performs it again, some of them can indeed create a chunk of useless infrastructure. Like regular infrastructure, this useless infrastructure has a tendency to attract demons who wish to gather aether. Voila - a demon summoning ritual! Use at your own risk, it also attracts stigmata and other dangerous creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T15:54:17-07:00","id":112987,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about that. Via the general mechanics of Infrastructure, it seems Angelic summoning is straight forward--create the infrastructure, summon an angel. But if you create that repeated, &quot;useless&quot; infrastructure.. it could be the target of Behind the Curtain. If the demon knows of this ritual infrastructure, he could jump to it from other infrastructure. In theory, a cultist could perform a ritual of summoning and end up calling forth an angel AND a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:13:38-07:00","id":113367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=112987#post112987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about that. Via the general mechanics of Infrastructure, it seems Angelic summoning is straight forward--create the infrastructure, summon an angel. But if you create that repeated, &quot;useless&quot; infrastructure.. it could be the target of Behind the Curtain. If the demon knows of this ritual infrastructure, he could jump to it from other infrastructure. In theory, a cultist could perform a ritual of summoning and end up calling forth an angel AND a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, or as a plot hook (think I'll just go add one to that thread) - summoning could be taken far less literally and demons could simply check out the infrastructure normally, rather than being summoned to it literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:02:30-07:00","id":113699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/109497-summoning-demons?p=112321#post112321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not simply say that summoning actually activates one of the many hidden subroutines that the GM wrote into reality. For whatever reason, the GM won't stop it or can't see its being used to summon demons (and other things). It can be one of the mysteries why normal people, demons, and other supernatural can use it, but angles cannot.<br /> <br /> As for groups, I can easily see uses for it. No reason only one demon may be called. A powerful demon creates a summons and sends out a call to multiple demons for unknown purposes with promises of high level covers and other things of value, perhaps something specific of value to each individual demon, they all agree and poof, your circle is filled with demons (group) from all over and you have the start of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very creative and very close to what I was conceptualizing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T08:26:47-07:00","id":125185,"title":"","content":"How to summon a demon - <br /> <br /> Setting up a ritual circle is creating temporary Infrastructure that a Demon can use Behind the Curtain to teleport to? Ritual incantation to call the Unchained's interest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}